{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the single callout in Section 8 (User Interaction) #}
{% set output_format_description = "a brief callout (1-2 sentences) highlighting the most impactful insight about user interaction requirements from the Section 8 data/insight, suitable for a distinct callout box" %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Review the data summary and chart insight provided below for "{{ section_title }}". This section focuses on the proportion of vulnerabilities requiring user interaction versus those directly exploitable.
Identify the *single most significant finding* for administrators regarding this trend. This could relate to the prevalence of social engineering tactics implied by user interaction, or conversely, the risk from directly exploitable flaws.
Craft a concise callout (1-2 sentences maximum) stating this key finding clearly and its potential implication for security posture (e.g., user training, patching urgency).
{% endblock task_instructions %}

